t_sha":"d7446eb4701c26f4de08b057394ffac70a7e2c24","position":"1788564489521815001-a7daf7fc-0630-4ea4-b141-430273410268"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6259395c09fcf5822dc7911dfad2b17a4323802dc662deac40c2e44a0fac6a03","event_uuid":"3cdbd256-ad83-4704-93cc-cdbdbd44838b","position":{"commit_sha":"ce308a54cf13ea7f8cbfa0924679d8008e393c7c","position":"1788564973547958001-3cdbd256-ad83-4704-93cc-cdbdbd44838b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4a134ef6588d0a9c791f24c6504e936d89c8d5c25519eb3f2b61d50c73ed085d","event_uuid":"2fc396de-6219-4035-92a0-b9febfe9a91e","position":{"commit_sha":"3889e8f2d156ff44d9fc6662f7ff42441b3f54b9","position":"1788564987714722001-2fc396de-6219-4035-92a0-b9febfe9a91e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix pushed as Gerrit change 2642 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2642), commit f71ddff402ea.\n\nRED evidence (before the fix), driving the real `Makefile` in a sandbox with `make venv` stubbed to exit 1:\n\n```\n→ git fetch origin\n→ git worktree add /tmp/.../wt -b demo origin/main\n→ provisioning /tmp/.../wt/.venv (pinned Python) then canonical 'make install'\n\n✓ worktree ready: /tmp/.../wt\n  activate it with:  cd /tmp/.../wt && source .venv/bin/activate\nEXIT=0\n```\n\n`make install` was never invoked (the delegation log recorded only `venv`), yet the target announced success and exited 0.\n\nThe new `tests/unit/test_makefile_worktree.py` was seen RED first: 4 failed / 1 passed (the surviving pass is the happy path, held as the guard against an \"always fail\" fix). After the `Makefile` change: 5 passed, and 12 passed together with `test_worktree_python_pin.py`.\n\nRoot cause confirmed as described in the plan: the recipe's steps were `;`-joined on one shell line and make checks only the line's overall status (its last command, an `echo`). Fixed with `set -e` plus per-step `|| { echo \"ERROR: …\"; exit 1; }` handlers naming the failed step; the provisioning handler also states the worktree exists but is unprovisioned and gives both the finish and the remove command.\n\nGates: `make lint` exit 0 (includes the complexity, mechanism-delta and repo hygiene ratchets), `make typecheck` exit 0. Per the operator's load constraint (the Gerrit host had a 41-minute IOPS outage tonight), the full local suite was deliberately NOT run; CI's `Verified` vote is the authoritative full-suite result.\n\nNot closing: awaiting `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` on change 2642.","timestamp":1788561532140783851},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Patch set 2 added a regression test for the `git fetch origin` failure handler, closing the single advisory the review bot raised on patch set 1 (that branch was the one named-handler without its own test). Confirmed RED against the pre-fix Makefile before landing it.\n\nGerrit change 2642 final state:\n- LLM-Review +1 (PASS, no findings) on patch set 2\n- Verified +1 on patch set 2 (https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/33927191139)\n- 0 unresolved comments\n- Status MERGED as 6c2267d8d7b1\n\nNOTE for the operator: this session did NOT submit the change. Gerrit records the submit at 23:23:51 under the `Rebar Bot Nava` identity, ~3 minutes after the `Verified +1` landed at 23:20:40, with no submit call from this session. Something else on this host running under the same Gerrit identity (an automation, or a concurrent agent session) submitted it. Worth confirming, since it means a change can land without the session that authored it deciding to land it.\n\nTicket deliberately left `in_progress` — the operator asked to close it themselves.","timestamp":1788564364776446551},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## CORRECTION: the submit at 23:23:51 was the ORCHESTRATOR, not an unknown automation\n\nThe implementing agent recorded that change 2642 was merged under the `Rebar Bot Nava` identity\nwithout it issuing a submit, and reasonably flagged that as a possible control failure — \"a change\ncan land without the session that authored it deciding to land it\".\n\n**That submit was mine.** As the orchestrating session I polled the Gerrit board, saw 2642 at\n`LLM-Review +1` / `Verified +1` with 0 unresolved comments, re-verified those labels directly\nvia `/a/changes/2642/detail?o=LABELS`, and issued `POST /a/changes/2642/submit`. It returned\nHTTP 200 with status MERGED. Both the orchestrator and its subagents authenticate as\n`RebarBotNava`, which is why the actor looked anonymous from inside the subagent.\n\nSo there is **no unauthorised automation**, and no missing control. The agent was right to flag it\ngiven what it could see — a merge it did not cause, under its own identity, is exactly the shape\nof a real problem — and wrong only because the orchestrator's actions are invisible to it.\n\nRecording this because an uncorrected \"something merges changes on its own\" note would cost a\nfuture reader a real investigation. It is also a genuine limitation worth knowing: subagents\ncannot distinguish orchestrator actions from third-party ones, since both wear the same Gerrit\nidentity. If that distinction ever needs to be auditable, it would take separate identities or an\nexplicit convention — not tracked here, and not needed today.\n\nThe division of labour was deliberate and unchanged: the agent implemented and pushed but did NOT\nsubmit and did NOT close, exactly as briefed. Submission and closure are the orchestrator's,\nperformed only after independently re-verifying both gate votes.","timestamp":1788564489521815001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788543316414949168,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"02c1608f-431c-4852-a862-213a4a574033","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"2af9-0769-6f23-41a8"},{"link_uuid":"04150a05-a61f-4d76-a09d-7b9f541615ef","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e4e6-a7d6-fe24-494e"},{"link_uuid":"1434a776-a322-4372-abb7-5a41ab8402f0","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1f21-a883-c233-4fd5"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`make worktree name=<branch>` creates the branch/worktree, but if its delegated `make venv && make install` step fails, the recipe continues, prints \"✓ worktree ready,\" and exits 0.\n\nObserved when an ambient `uv` violated the repository's pinned expectation: `make venv` failed and no `.venv` existed, yet the target reported success. The agent then works in a worktree with no `ruff`/`mypy`, and the pre-commit gate fails at commit time with `make: mypy: No such file or directory` — which reads as a code problem rather than an environment one.\n\nThis is the \"absence of execution reported as success\" defect class: provisioning did not happen, and the exit status said it did.\n\n## Root cause\n`Makefile:198` `worktree:` executes its provisioning as a single shell line whose commands are joined with `;`, and make does **not** apply `set -e` semantics inside a recipe line (make only checks the exit status of the whole line, i.e. of the last command in the list). Verified in the tree at `Makefile` lines 211-220:\n\n```\n\tgit fetch origin; \\\n\tgit worktree add \"$$target_dir\" -b \"$(name)\" origin/main; \\\n\t( cd \"$$target_dir\" && $(MAKE) venv && . .venv/bin/activate && $(MAKE) install ); \\\n\techo \"\"; \\\n\techo \"✓ worktree ready: $$target_dir\"; \\\n```\n\nThe provisioning subshell's non-zero status is discarded by the following `;`, and the line's status becomes that of the final `echo` — zero. The sibling `venv:` target (`Makefile` lines 188-196) already gets this right by using `|| { …; exit 1; }` explicitly, so the fix is to bring `worktree:` to the same standard.\n\n## Approach\nMake the `worktree:` recipe line fail-fast and make each failure name itself:\n\n1. Prefix the recipe line with `set -e` so every command in the list aborts the line (portable POSIX-shell behaviour; make runs recipes under `/bin/sh` by default, so this needs no GNU-only feature and no CI provider).\n2. Wrap each of the three fallible steps — `git fetch origin`, `git worktree add`, and the provisioning subshell — in an explicit `|| { echo \"ERROR: …\"; exit 1; }` that names the step that failed and (for provisioning) tells the reader the worktree exists but is unprovisioned and how to finish or remove it. The explicit handlers are what makes the failure loud; `set -e` is the belt-and-braces that catches anything added later without a handler.\n3. The `✓ worktree ready` message stays where it is; because the line now aborts, it is only reachable after provisioning succeeds.\n\nChosen over restructuring the target into separate recipe lines (one per step, letting make's own per-line status checking do the work) because the recipe carries a shell variable `target_dir` across all its steps; make runs each recipe line in its own shell, so splitting would require recomputing or exporting that variable in every line — more moving parts for the same guarantee.\n\n## Scope\n- `Makefile` — the `worktree:` target only (`set -e` + per-step error handlers). No other target changes.\n- `tests/unit/test_makefile_worktree.py` — new regression test.\n\n## Testing\nThe regression test drives the **real** `Makefile` in a throwaway `tmp_path` sandbox, following the sandbox pattern already used by `tests/unit/test_worktree_python_pin.py::_sandbox` (which copies the Makefile into `tmp_path` and prepends a stub-bin directory to `PATH`). Two stubs isolate the recipe's control flow from the host: a stub `git` on `PATH` (recording, and creating the target directory on `worktree add`), and the delegated provisioning stubbed by passing `MAKE=<stub>` as a command-line variable, which overrides the `$(MAKE)` the recipe expands. The stub `make` records its argument and exits with a caller-chosen status, and on a successful `venv` creates a `.venv/bin/activate` so the recipe's `.` sourcing step behaves. No real worktree, branch, network fetch, venv, or `uv`/`pre-commit` invocation happens, so the tests are subprocess-fast and leave nothing on the host.\n\n- Failure path (the bug): `git` stubbed to succeed, provisioning stubbed to fail. Assert `make worktree` exits non-zero, that its combined output does **not** contain the `✓ worktree ready` success message, and that it does contain an `ERROR:` line naming provisioning.\n- Failure path (earlier step): `git worktree add` stubbed to exit non-zero. Assert non-zero exit and no success message.\n- Happy path: every stub succeeds. Assert exit 0 and that the success message is printed — so the fix cannot be \"always fail\".\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] With provisioning stubbed to fail, `make worktree name=<x> dir=<tmp>` exits non-zero — verified by the new test asserting `returncode != 0`.\n- [x] In that same failing run the string `✓ worktree ready` is absent from stdout+stderr, and an `ERROR:` line naming the failed step is present — verified by the new test's output assertions.\n- [x] With `git worktree add` stubbed to fail, `make worktree` exits non-zero — verified by the new test.\n- [x] With every step stubbed to succeed, `make worktree` still exits 0 and prints the success message — verified by the new test.\n- [x] The regression test creates no real worktree, branch, or venv outside its sandbox — verified by the test running entirely under `tmp_path` with a stub `git` on `PATH` and a stubbed `$(MAKE)`, so no `git worktree add`, `uv`, or network call reaches the host.\n- [x] `make lint` and `make typecheck` exit 0.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"Makefile","reason":"the worktree target that reports success after provisioning failure"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_makefile_worktree.py","reason":"new regression test pinning that a provisioning failure is reported as failure"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","1f21-a883-c233-4fd5"],["relates_to","e4e6-a7d6-fe24-494e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"3cdbd256-ad83-4704-93cc-cdbdbd44838b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["bootstrap","developer-experience","makefile"],"ticket_id":"1738-3816-caca-44a2","ticket_type":"bug","title":"make worktree reports success after provisioning failure","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f5ba7220-61fc-4389-b88e-099597e95c70","a2deee13-e166-4c45-9cca-456af1cf52a9","c510f150-3fb9-45fb-9b60-ed14b5f4c1cf","73c83eb2-baa0-4727-bb6c-e2b43c89dd60","0d3532c5-459c-4c3f-8a00-0332a2294c40","03ac495d-75b7-48fa-a4f0-29654576a9cb","04150a05-a61f-4d76-a09d-7b9f541615ef","1434a776-a322-4372-abb7-5a41ab8402f0","05baae47-62cf-408d-ac08-2bc383e7caf2","2cf78284-e1a0-41d0-ab0f-13d21784834